ure":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commit/edb342d65c31863d96167e4b63e7d5f067df3df1","node_id":"C_kwDOQov0ktoAKGVkYjM0MmQ2NWMzMTg2M2Q5NjE2N2U0YjYzZTdkNWYwNjdkZjNkZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commit/3e8f48f1bf911d1c2ec5dcb7fbb01ce03f72a918","sha":"3e8f48f1bf911d1c2ec5dcb7fbb01ce03f72a918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/3e8f48f1bf911d1c2ec5dcb7fbb01ce03f72a918"}],"sha":"edb342d65c31863d96167e4b63e7d5f067df3df1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/edb342d65c31863d96167e4b63e7d5f067df3df1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/3e8f48f1bf911d1c2ec5dcb7fbb01ce03f72a918/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T03:03:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T03:03:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"chore(landing): honesty audit — align all landing copy with what''s shipped\n\nApplied the confirmed findings from an adversarial multi-agent audit of every\nrouted landing surface (each finding verified by a skeptic agent + render-path\ntrace before change). Scope: v2 sections, v1 public pages (/about /contact\n/privacy /security /terms /legal/accessibility), shared footer, and the\nreduced-motion hero mock.\n\nHighlights:\n- Hero lede no longer claims \"family communication\" (messaging is unshipped) —\n  it contradicted the same page''s \"in development\" pillar. Now: finance.\n- Fabricated attribution removed: the District lede no longer credits a made-up\n  three-trait list to the World Bank SABER framework (SABER defines four\n  national-EMIS policy areas, not this list) — restated as our own thesis.\n- Platform pillars corrected to shipped scope: Core (guardians, not\n  \"discipline\"), Finance (fee structures/invoices/payments/family billing, not\n  \"budgets/payroll/vendor management\"), Scheduling (academic years/sections/bell\n  schedules/BS+AD dates), API (CSV export today; public API/GraphQL/SSO roadmap),\n  heading \"One data model\" (dropped \"Six modules\").\n- Security honesty: dropped unverifiable claims across v2 SecurityStrip and the\n  v1 Security page — no \"TLS 1.3\"/\"keys rotate automatically\", no \"regular\n  penetration testing\", no \"MFA available\", no \"immutable audit trails\", no\n  \"geographically redundant backups\"; compliance badges changed from green\n  \"Compliant/Ready\" check-circles to \"by design\" framing (FERPA/COPPA/GDPR),\n  SSDPC badge removed, \"Encrypted end-to-end\" → \"at rest and in transit\".\n- FAQ + About + Terms + Privacy + Accessibility: no \"communications/scheduling\"\n  as shipped, no \"human resources\", no \"AI-ready\", no \"K-12 and districts\", no\n  \"WCAG 2.1 AA on every release\" (→ \"working toward\"); privacy dates + FERPA/\n  COPPA sections reframed as design intent for US schools; fixed a dead\n  accessibility@ mailto → shoaibrain@edforge.net; \"onboarding early partner\n  schools\" → \"live with our first pilot in Nepal\".\n- Footer: removed dead \"#\" nav items (Documentation, Changelog, Careers, Press,\n  Principals) and non-shipped \"products\" (Communications, Platform & API);\n  columns now point to real anchors/routes. Compliance line → \"Privacy by\n  design (FERPA / COPPA) · Ed-Fi Aligned\".\n- Reduced-motion hero mock: \"Messages / awaiting a reply\" KPI → \"Exams\";\n  \"Fee reminders sent\" → \"Fee invoices issued\".\n- Tests updated in lockstep (SABER, \"Six modules\").\n\nDeliberately NOT changed (needs owner input): the X/Twitter handle\n@edforgedotnet on the Contact page — verify it exists before launch, else remove.\n\nGates: turbo typecheck pass, lint 0 errors, vitest landing 194/194.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e3f39ddc148e9f842745fae21fa4ff8708864b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/git/trees/1e3f39ddc148e9f842745fae21fa4ff8708864b6"},"ur