2a5ab13bde2c5a9366a2cb39d749b5","sha":"148bea94402a5ab13bde2c5a9366a2cb39d749b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/148bea94402a5ab13bde2c5a9366a2cb39d749b5"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commit/5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2","sha":"5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2"}],"sha":"caaa60bee368c5e5a3572411644a9167364e40a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/caaa60bee368c5e5a3572411644a9167364e40a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T20:03:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T20:03:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(shell): draw content-pane focus ring inset so its top edge shows\n\nThe app content pane (`<main id=\"main-content\" tabIndex={-1}>`) is\nprogrammatically focused on every route change, so it wears the platform\nkeyboard-focus ring (the brand-green `[tabindex]:focus-visible` outline in\npackages/theme utilities.css). That ring uses `outline-offset: 2px`, painting\n2px *outside* the element.\n\nThe pane sits flush under the fixed topbar — the body wrap uses `pt-0`, so\nthere is no page-background gutter above the card (unlike the 12px gutter on\nthe left/right/bottom). The fixed `z-45` header, filled with the opaque page\nbackground, spans y=0..56px and paints above the in-flow `<main>`, occluding\nthe ring''s top segment. Result: the focus outline is visible on three sides\nbut its top edge disappears under the header.\n\nFix: a single shell-scoped rule overrides only the offset for this pane\n(`#main-content:focus-visible { outline-offset: -2px }`) so the ring paints\njust inside the pane edge, clear of the header, on all four sides. Width and\nthe `--border-focus` color still come from the shared platform rule — the\ntoken source is unchanged, and no other focus ring in the app is affected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X4NJCPBbJc6J3URE2xs9E1","tree":{"sha":"132e4fad761c8916bd5a81489e9cea92f0e1a1ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/git/trees/132e4fad761c8916bd5a81489e9cea92f0e1a1ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/git/commits/5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 132e4fad761c8916bd5a81489e9cea92f0e1a1ca\nparent b573e59bfa08727a5fd2daa3b91e72d92b16d97f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783109002 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783109002 +0000\n\nfix(shell): draw content-pane focus ring inset so its top edge shows\n\nThe app content pane (`<main id=\"main-content\" tabIndex={-1}>`) is\nprogrammatically focused on every route change, so it wears the platform\nkeyboard-focus ring (the brand-green `[tabindex]:focus-visible` outline in\npackages/theme utilities.css). That ring uses `outline-offset: 2px`, painting\n2px *outside* the element.\n\nThe pane sits flush under the fixed topbar — the body wrap uses `pt-0`, so\nthere is no page-background gutter above the card (unlike the 12px gutter on\nthe left/right/bottom). The fixed `z-45` header, filled with the opaque page\nbackground, spans y=0..56px and paints above the in-flow `<main>`, occluding\nthe ring''s top segment. Result: the focus outline is visible on three sides\nbut its top edge disappears under the header.\n\nFix: a single shell-scoped rule overrides only the offset for this pane\n(`#main-content:focus-visible { outline-offset: -2px }`) so the ring paints\njust inside the pane edge, clear of the header, on all four sides. Width and\nthe `--border-focus` color still come from the shared platform rule — the\ntoken source is unchanged, and no other focus ring in the app is affected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X4NJCPBbJc6J3URE2xs9E1\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEmOSDVt\nxk/UqplH8e/vUGsCoK+zN+2ikHxMbA/q8wuaOoCsAcDdj6rQZlNTuJOIIkp/HqIVQFz5w7w0x1wh\nVgI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-03T20:03:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commit/5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2","node_id":"C_kwDOQov0ktoAKDVjZTk4YjExOWUxZmM4NWVmOGY3ZDBjMmEyY2QwZTFiM2MxODM2YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commit/b573e59bfa08727a5fd2daa3b91e72d92b16d97f","sha":"b573e59bfa08727a5fd2daa3b91e72d92b16d97f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/b573e59bfa08727a5fd2daa3b91e72d92b16d97f"}],"sha":"5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/5ce98b119e1fc85ef8f7d0c2a2cd0e1b3c1836a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/05086630920c9acd42bb05a7ff8e34da54a6774f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T19:32:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T19:32:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(finance): polish bulk-export drawer UX — honest progress, contained spinner, soft borders, background toast\n\nFive fixes from the export-flow screen recording review:\n\n1. Busy icon: the header tile''s spinner was a rotating rounded-SQUARE\n   ring whose corners swept outside the tile (a rotating square''s\n   footprint exceeds its bounds). Replaced with a circular track+arc\n   ring inscribed in the tile — a circle''s footprint is rotation-\n   invariant, so nothing can bleed. motion-reduce hides it.\n\n2. Honest progress: the worker flushes counters in batches of 25\n   (COUNTER_BATCH_SIZE), so sub-25-doc exports poll 0% until terminal.\n   ExportRunning now renders an INDETERMINATE sweep bar + stage text\n   (\"Preparing export…\" / \"Generating PDFs…\") until the first real\n   counter lands, then switches to a true percentage with\n   \"N of M PDFs prepared\" and the counters card. The fake current-\n   file ticker (derived from a stuck counter) is removed. New\n   v2-indeterminate-sweep keyframe degrades to a static low-opacity\n   fill under prefers-reduced-motion.\n\n3. Soft borders: dark-mode border tokens are pure white and meant for\n   low-opacity use; the drawer chrome and export cards used them at\n   full strength. Moved to the house /0.35 (dividers, chips) and /0.5\n   (card edges, tiles) convention — ui Drawer panel edge + header/\n   footer dividers included, so all drawers get the calmer chrome.\n\n4. Phase transitions: preflight → running → result/failed now\n   crossfade (AnimatePresence mode=\"wait\", 150ms, ±8px y; offset\n   zeroed under reduced motion) instead of hard-swapping.\n\n5. Completion toast: it only ever fired while the drawer was open on\n   the result view (redundant + overlapping the Download footer), and\n   \"Run in background\" silently killed the poll because the callers\n   unmounted the drawer on close. Drawers are now mounted\n   unconditionally, state resets on the open transition (keeping a\n   live job attached), and the toast fires only when the drawer is\n   closed — with a Download action — making the \"runs in background,\n   we''ll let you know\" note true.\n\nAlso refreshed the stale \"Download PDF (ZIP)\" toolbar labels to\n\"Download PDFs\" (the picker now offers merged PDF too, #305).\n\nVerified: turbo typecheck, lint, vitest 1345 passed, 8/8 e2e @smoke,\nplus a scripted Playwright walk of both flows (watched + backgrounded)\nin dark/light and reduced-motion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019AcJB4ZKWCti6W8tVCgskt","tree":{"sha":"4526677bc46b3ae7256f81042c64231bd14d6535","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/git/trees/4526677bc46b3ae7256f81042c64231bd14d6535"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/git/commits/05086630920c9acd42bb05a7ff8e34da54a6774f","verification":{"payload":"tree 4526677bc46b3ae7256f81042c64231bd14d6535\nparent 9f57be2580b30ba7686f286fbb486dedf0f43e6c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783107172 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783107172 +0000\n\nfix(finance): polish bulk-export drawer UX — honest progress, contained spinner, soft borders, background toast\n\nFive fixes from the export-flow screen recording review:\n\n1. Busy icon: the header tile''s spinner was a rotating rounded-SQUARE\n   ring whose corners swept outside the tile (a rotating square''s\n   footprint exceeds its bounds). Replaced with a circular track+arc\n   ring inscribed in the tile — a circle''s footprint is rotation-\n   invariant, so nothing can bleed. motion-reduce hides it.\n\n2. Honest progress: the worker flushes counters in batches of 25\n   (COUNTER_BATCH_SIZE), so sub-25-doc exports poll 0% until terminal.\n   ExportRunning now renders an INDETERMINATE sweep bar + stage text\n   (\"Preparing export…\" / \"Generating PDFs…\") until the first real\n   counter lands, then switches to a true percentage with\n   \"N of M PDFs prepared\" and the counters card. The fake current-\n   file ticker (derived from a stuck counter) is removed. New\n   v2-indeterminate-sweep keyframe degrades to a static low-opacity\n   fill under prefers-reduced-motion.\n\n3. Soft borders: dark-mode border tokens are pure white and meant for\n   low-opacity use; the drawer chrome and export cards used them at\n   full strength. Moved to the house /0.35 (dividers, chips) and /0.5\n   (card edges, tiles) convention — ui Drawer panel edge + header/\n   footer dividers included, so all drawers get the calmer chrome.\n\n4. Phase transitions: preflight → running → result/failed now\n   crossfade (AnimatePresence mode=\"wait\", 150ms, ±8px y; offset\n   zeroed under reduced motion) instead of hard-swapping.\n\n5. Completion toast: it only ever fired while the drawer was open on\n   the result view (redundant + overlapping the Download footer), and\n   \"Run in background\" silently killed the poll because the callers\n   unmounted the drawer on close. Drawers are now mounted\n   unconditionally, state resets on the open transition (keeping a\n   live job attached), and the toast fires only when the drawer is\n   closed — with a Download action — making the \"runs in background,\n   we''ll let you know\" note true.\n\nAlso refreshed the stale \"Download PDF (ZIP)\" toolbar labels to\n\"Download PDFs\" (the picker now offers merged PDF too, #305).\n\nVerified: turbo typecheck, lint, vitest 1345 passed, 8/8 e2e @smoke,\nplus a scripted Playwright walk of both flows (watched + backgrounded)\nin dark/light and reduced-motion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019AcJB4ZKWCti6W8tVCgskt\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQABDjAGD\nFBzgvV2TgEPbh8biACtgC9KqsSfZTW34wvNql8lw2qTddW9Bi51ETxFHarQxE3ZbJyk6jkyhgxjH\nwQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-03T19:33:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commit/05086630920c9acd42bb05a7ff8e34da54a6774f","node_id":"C_kwDOQov0ktoAKDA1MDg2NjMwOTIwYzlhY2Q0MmJiMDVhN2ZmOGUzNGRhNTRhNjc3NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commit/9f57be2580b30ba7686f286fbb486dedf0f43e6c","sha":"9f57be2580b30ba7686f286fbb486dedf0f43e6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend/commits/9f57be2580b30ba7686f286fbb486dedf0f43e6c"}],"sha":"05086630920c9acd42bb05a7ff8e34da54a6774f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sh