ekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/799dc49d67247676c1edff7ba6236689b1053313","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDc5OWRjNDlkNjcyNDc2NzZjMWVkZmY3YmE2MjM2Njg5YjEwNTMzMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5","sha":"4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5"}],"sha":"799dc49d67247676c1edff7ba6236689b1053313","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/799dc49d67247676c1edff7ba6236689b1053313"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T17:25:48Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T17:25:48Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Proposals take the member''s category. This was the one that mattered most, because it was silently disabling the previous two turns'' work. The petition routes discarded any submitted topic and classified from body text — and with no gardener or classifying extension installed, the classifier only ever returns the first anchor. So on a default deployment every proposal landed on general: topic-scoped delegation, category filters and breadcrumbs all collapsed into one bucket, and the category hierarchy had nothing to match against. Compose and draft-edit now carry a Category field with the shared topic datalist; the member''s pick is authoritative, an edit that omits it keeps the existing category, and the classifier stays as the fallback.\n\nLane-moderator role. Sits between member and admin: can act on what the lanes carry (promote, decide requests), cannot touch what defines the group (policy, categories, delegates, roles). A group can never be left without an admin.\n\nPromotion requests. An ordinary member can now ask instead of hitting a wall. Visible to the group, auditable, decidable only by someone who could promote — never the asker — declinable with a reason that reaches them, and it can''t stack. An approval blocked by a closed parent lane leaves the request open rather than silently consuming the ask.\n\nBranch election roll-up. Opt-in and parent-side. A parent adopts a descendant''s closed election only for a category it hasn''t voted on itself, resolved at read time so a re-election is reflected immediately, and labelled with the branch it came from — a branch''s vote presented as the parent''s own would bind people who never joined it. The group''s own election always wins.\n\nThe end-to-end payoff, verified live\nA member delegates only the parent category Energy. Someone files a proposal under Energy / Solar. Her ballot resolves to @bruno.sala and reads \"awaiting their vote (5 days left)\", with the tally showing awaiting delegates: 1 separate from the abstentions.\n\nEvery link in that chain was broken three turns ago: the proposal would have been general, the parent delegation wouldn''t have matched it, and the ballot would have counted as a silent abstention forever.\n\nAlso confirmed live: a plain member''s request → blocked second request → blocked self-approval → lane moderator approves → item moves to the party lane → asker notified.","tree":{"sha":"f3553fe1d6709b87fae283325095fd5b0dc72343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/f3553fe1d6709b87fae283325095fd5b0dc72343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDRjNmEyZGYxNjI3ODI2YjA2YzY1ZmFiZGZmNmRhYzIwODM5YjA4YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66","sha":"81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66"}],"sha":"4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/4c6a2df1627826b06c65fabdff6dac20839b08a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T17:06:09Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T17:06:09Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Subgroups (note #3). A group can be a branch of another — a party with a think tank, a working wing, an alternative line — with a depth cap, self/cycle guards, lineage on the card, and a tree-ordered list. Nesting is deliberately structural, not authority: a branch doesn''t inherit its parent''s membership and isn''t governed by it. What it buys is discovery, a defined \"upper level\", and specificity — a branch cachet settles a delegation tie its parent''s can''t, but never overrides an explicit priority.\n\nGroup categories + discovery (notes #2, #5). Groups declare categories, registered through the same nested topic registry the site uses, so Energy / Solar declared by a branch is the category a delegation can be scoped to. /groups gained a category directory — each category, the groups covering it, who they put forward (cachet or election winner), one-click delegate. That''s the discovery path topic-scoped delegation was missing: members were told delegation is per-category, then handed a free-text box.\n\nOptional internal lanes (note #6). Per-group discussion and proposal lanes, off by default, members-only or public to read. They reuse /discussion and /petitions via a ?group= scope rather than duplicating them — so pagination, evidence, stances, quorum, votes and last turn''s delegated ballots all work inside a group with no second implementation. Group entries are excluded from the Circle feed; that subtraction is the whole of what makes a lane internal.\n\nPromote to upper level (note #7). Moves an item to the parent group, or to the Circle when top-level. A move, not a copy — the item keeps its id, so its comments, signatures and votes travel with it instead of forking into two records of one decision.\n\nTwo bugs the live walkthrough caught that the unit tests didn''t\nA permission gate that was open. In evaluatePromotion I attached the resolved group to refusals via ...resolved — placed after ok: false. Since resolved is itself an ok: true result, the spread overwrote the refusal into an approval, and a non-member successfully promoted another group''s discussion. My test asserted .error (correctly set) rather than .ok, so it passed while the gate stood open. Fixed with a refuse() builder that keeps the verdict authoritative; tests now assert ok, that the item doesn''t move, and that guests are refused.\n\nHierarchical matching missed the natural way to type a path. A member typing Energy / Solar stores energy / solar with spaces, but match keys join as energy/solar — so nothing matched and the chain view read \"No effective delegations resolved\". Last turn''s tests only used unspaced paths. Both sides now canonicalize through canonicalizeTopicKey.\n\nBoth were only visible by driving the real thing; I''ve noted the pattern in AGENTS so the next agent doesn''t rebuild either trap.","tree":{"sha":"fe062adeea4d43b3e9b6930f89819fd47d0e4936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/fe062adeea4d43b3e9b6930f89819fd47d0e4936"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDgxMTU3Y2Q1YzM5OTE5NDcxZGRkMzgyODA2N2NhZjNhOTAxYjFlNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135","sha":"9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135"}],"sha":"81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/81157cd5c39919471ddd3828067caf3a901b1e66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:41:54Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T16:41:54Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Delegation didn''t do anything. A delegated vote was stored as the literal string delegate:<hash>, and the tally only understood yes/no/abstain — so every delegated ballot fell into the abstain bucket and stayed there. Members could set delegates, see chains, get election winners, and none of it moved a single vote.\n\nVote topic category → Delegate, with override and a window:\n\nA delegated ballot is now a structured record (choice: ''delegate'' + a delegate binding), resolved at read time through the delegate''s own vote, transitively, under the existing cycle/depth guards.\ndelegateVoteWindowDays (governance, default 5, 0 = no deadline) is how long the delegate has. Editable in /admin and proposable by members at /governance.\nA ballot inside its window is reported as pending, deliberately not folded into the abstentions — counting it as an abstention would misreport the outcome while the delegate can still act. Only lapsed or unresolvable ballots become abstentions.\nThe member overrides any time by voting themselves; that replaces the ballot outright.\nVerified live: giulia hands her ballot to marco → tally reads abstain: 0 · awaiting delegates: 1; marco votes yes → yes: 2. Before this change that would have been yes: 1 · abstain: 1.\n\nNote #2/#4 — categories and subcategories\nTopic matching was exact-string, so a delegation on environment never applied to a proposal filed under environment/energy — which is most of them, since proposals are classified into nested paths. Resolution now walks narrowest-first (environment/energy → energy → environment → general), so a parent-category delegation covers subcategories while a more specific one still wins. Same rule for forwarding hops, group cachets, and group elections — so a branch group''s subcategory election outranks the parent''s general one.\n\nUX both sides of the contract\n/delegation gained \"Ballots waiting on your vote\" (the delegate''s inbox, with countdowns) and \"Votes riding on a delegate\" (the member''s, with override links). /petitions states who holds your ballot, how long they have, whether it''s been counted; the vote button reads \"Override\". The delegate is notified when a ballot arrives; you''re notified when your delegate votes.\n\nTwo things worth flagging\nI found a gap that blunts the hierarchy work. The petition create route ignores a submitted topic entirely and classifies from body text — and with no gardener or classifying extension, every proposal lands on general. So on a default deployment the nested matching has nothing to match against. /discussion honours its topic input; petitions doesn''t, and has no topic field in its compose form. I logged it in OPTIMIZATIONS rather than fixing it, since changing proposal classification is a separate decision — but it''s the thing to do next if you want the category work to be visible.","tree":{"sha":"60d041ffa55c4df2dbbac75310c9d3aadec87a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/60d041ffa55c4df2dbbac75310c9d3aadec87a47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDljYmJlMDE4YzYzMDQ2MWNlYzYxMTZjZjIyMGFmN2ViNDU2YjgxMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f","sha":"12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f"}],"sha":"9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/9cbbe018c630461cec6116cf220af7eb456b8135"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/3b539b333363b7c09543934390556c68ced21a36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:45:24Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:45:24Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Merge branch ''main'' of https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web","tree":{"sha":"9d10a86c6d123217117d9e675533d7001eafa1cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/9d10a86c6d123217117d9e675533d7001eafa1cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/3b539b333363b7c09543934390556c68ced21a36","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/3b539b333363b7c09543934390556c68ced21a36","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDNiNTM5YjMzMzM2M2I3YzA5NTQzOTM0MzkwNTU2YzY4Y2VkMjFhMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f","sha":"12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/5f9e3f9d9b570c44df4078113f19776408c8d17f","sha":"5f9e3f9d9b570c44df4078113f19776408c8d17f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/5f9e3f9d9b570c44df4078113f19776408c8d17f"}],"sha":"3b539b333363b7c09543934390556c68ced21a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/3b539b333363b7c09543934390556c68ced21a36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:40:45Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:40:45Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Complete the modern structure rollout across the remaining surfaces\n\nFinishes UI_ROADMAP backlog item 4. Every member-facing route now uses the\nexemplar .page-grid shape - content in .page-main, short controls in the rail.\n\n/governance keeps the published constitution and the proposal/decision history\nin the main column and moves the long change-proposal form to the rail, so the\ncurrent values sit beside you while you propose changes to them. /delegation\nleads with your delegations and their resolved chains, with the set/clear form\nand group recommendations in the rail. /delegates puts the people list first and\nsearch in the rail, and the delegate profile keeps the accountability record -\ncoverage, votes, activity - in the main column with endorsements and election\nwins alongside. /groups, /notifications and /profile follow the same split;\nprofile now leads with identity rather than provider-local attributes.\n\n/admin was a single 742-line template and is now 7 grouped partials - setup,\nmodules, policy, structure, federation, observability, operations - which closes\nthe standing template-hygiene item. All 20 of its panels are section-tagged and\nlabelled, so they are hideable server-side and read properly in the member\nSections control rather than falling back to heading text. The rendered output\nwas diffed against the previous template: every panel and every content line is\npreserved, with only panel order changing where the grouping regrouped them.\n\n/admin deliberately stays single-column. The reference \"dashboard shell\" is a\npersistent left sidebar plus a main column, which the app already has in the\nshared side-nav, and a settings page whose 20 panels are each a jump target\nreads better as one column than split across a rail.\n\nVerified per UIReview across 13 routes x 2 themes: zero WCAG-AA contrast\nfailures, zero horizontal overflow, every panel labelled. Full suite 210 passed,\n0 failed, 3 skipped; both smoke scripts and the Scenario A replay pass.\n\nThe sweep that checks contrast and overflow is still an ad-hoc script rather\nthan part of the suite - logged in OPTIMIZATIONS.md, along with lazy-rendering\nthe heavyweight admin panels, which the decomposition now makes straightforward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40a3df31846b12af2eb26c58085d1b261b816707","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/40a3df31846b12af2eb26c58085d1b261b816707"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDEyNjM5YzFlZmY4NGJjZTBkZmEzMWRjZDM2NzdiY2VkNWRjZGI0NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934","sha":"0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934"}],"sha":"12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/12639c1eff84bce0dfa31dcd3677bced5dcdb44f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:25:28Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T14:25:28Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Roll the modern structure out to discussion, petitions and organization\n\nContinues UI_ROADMAP backlog item 4, one surface per pass.\n\n/discussion and /petitions were still stacked full-width panels with the\ncompose form above the content, and carried no section tags at all, so the\nmember \"Sections\" control was empty on both. Both now use the exemplar\n.page-grid shape - content in .page-main, short controls in the rail - and are\ndecomposed into templates/partials/, which is also the standing template-hygiene\nitem. /organization''s full-width marketing hero becomes a compact workspace\nstrip with its prose moved to is-verbose, so the pressure inbox sits above the\nfold as the AGENTS contract has always required.\n\nTwo layout defects surfaced while rolling this out, both affecting the shipped\nexemplar as much as the new surfaces.\n\nThe aside rail could not hold a tall panel. With max-height + overflow:auto an\nexpanded compose form was clipped so its own submit button sat outside the\nrail''s visible box. The obvious alternative is worse: a sticky element taller\nthan the viewport pins at `top` and then stops moving, so everything below the\nfold becomes permanently unreachable - scrolling the page does not help. Either\nway the member cannot submit the form. The rail is now a plain column, the\nnow-unused .sticky-panel class is removed, and a test asserts the submit button\nis reachable on every compose surface at 800x600. It was verified to fail\nagainst the previous CSS rather than assumed to work.\n\nThe page grid also collapsed on the wrong measurement. Keyed to the viewport, it\nignored the ~240px side-nav, so at a ~850px viewport the main column was\nsqueezed to ~160px while the aside kept its full 360px - on /forum and\n/social/feed too. .shell main now declares container-type: inline-size and the\ngrid collapses via @container shell-main, so the main column never drops below\n~425px before stacking. The old media query stays as a fallback.\n\nThe organization template test asserted the exact marketing headline that was\nthe thing OPTIMIZATIONS flagged as wrong; it now asserts the workspace title and\nthe \"Illustrative case data\" honesty cue, which is the durable contract.\n\nFull suite: 210 passed, 0 failed, 3 skipped. Both smoke scripts pass, the\nScenario A replay passes, and the WCAG AA sweep is still clean on all 13 routes\nin both themes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef2ae5475b36e92591e4611cc242184328125211","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/ef2ae5475b36e92591e4611cc242184328125211"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDBmODk2NDc0ZGY3MjM4Yzc3NGEzNDg0NTg5NjFlNGUwZDRhMTM5MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b","sha":"48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b"}],"sha":"0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/0f896474df7238c774a348458961e4e0d4a13934"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T13:44:04Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T13:44:04Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Ship light/system themes, label every section, unify appearance vocabulary\n\nCompletes the top three items of the UI_ROADMAP backlog.\n\nLight + system themes. Component CSS still carried ~150 theme-blind rgba()/hex\nliterals (recessed wells, hairlines, a fixed mint marker), so a light palette\nlaid on top would have rendered black panels on a white page. Convert those\nfamilies into HSL channel triplets first, letting a rule keep its own alpha\nwhile the theme owns the colour, then re-declare only the neutral/status/\noverlay block under :root[data-theme=\"light\"]. The accent engine still derives\nfrom --primary-h, so every accent preset works in both themes. The migration is\nlossless: each family resolves to the exact rgba() it replaced, and a\nselector-keyed computed-style diff across 12 routes shows dark mode unchanged\napart from the deliberate fixes below.\n\n\"system\" is resolved by a prefers-color-scheme media query rather than\nJavaScript, so it applies on the first paint and with JS disabled. Plain CSS\ncannot share a declaration body between a bare selector and a media-query-\nscoped one, so the light palette is written twice and a test asserts the two\nblocks stay identical.\n\nContrast is verified rather than assumed: every member-facing route now passes\nWCAG AA in both themes. That also cleared three pre-existing dark-mode\nfailures - avatar discs (blue hues sat at 4.08:1), the stance--question and\nstance--neutral chips (3.5:1, now on a new --primary-ink token for text on\naccent-tinted fills), and stance--proposal, which was pinned to a fixed violet\nand stopped matching once a member repicked their accent.\n\nSection labels. All 36 chrome-bearing panels carry data-section-label, enforced\nby a test so a new panel cannot ship unlabeled. Two findings: the\nnotifications preferences panel was never tagged because it is rendered from a\ncontroller string rather than a template, and the member Sections list was\noffering the Composer''s synthesized panel-N keys. Those are index-derived (so\nthey move when a page changes shape) and unknown server-side, meaning hiding\none silently did not survive SSR; they are now flagged and excluded.\n\nAppearance vocabulary. The layout ships data-ui-vocabulary from\ninterfaceSettings.js and app.js reads it, so the accent/density/theme key lists\ncan no longer drift between server and browser.\n\nAlso repairs two dev smoke scripts that were already failing on main:\nui-smoke.js asserted that / redirects a verified session to /social/feed, which\nwas deliberately removed when home became an operational workspace, and\nui-composer-smoke.js asserted pre-rename nav labels. The composer script now\nlocates the side-nav group by its stable data-composer-key, which is what let a\nrename degrade the assertion into an empty list instead of a failure. Neither\nscript runs in npm test, which is why both rotted unnoticed - logged in\nOPTIMIZATIONS.md along with the rotated section keys in profile.html and\ndelegate-profile.html, which need a migration before they can be renamed.\n\nFull suite: 209 passed, 0 failed, 3 skipped (external adapters unconfigured).\nBoth smoke scripts and the Scenario A replay pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8760735619200a26948e3412148d4fdc1c3c4e40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/8760735619200a26948e3412148d4fdc1c3c4e40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDQ4ZTViY2QzZWRiZWU0N2Q0NjQ5NmI5NzJjOTBmMDdlNmIyOTdiNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84","sha":"5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84"}],"sha":"48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/48e5bcd3edbee47d46496b972c90f07e6b297b6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T10:59:55Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T10:59:55Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Regenerate README walkthrough screenshots from scenario replays\n\nRe-executed party-journeys.js (Scenario A) and user-journeys.js against fresh\nstandalone stores, driving both reference scenarios end-to-end through the UI\nwith all step assertions passing, and refreshed the embedded README media.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68d5ab81f10472e953f846bf8524910cc283384c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/68d5ab81f10472e953f846bf8524910cc283384c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDVlMzQxOGY5NjRjOGM2NTU2Zjk2YTM2ZWJlNDkzOWQ2ZWJmYzNhODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731","sha":"55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731"}],"sha":"5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/5e3418f964c8c6556f96a36ebe4939d6ebfc3a84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T10:50:34Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T10:50:34Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Modernize UI with HSL tokens and member appearance/section controls\n\nAdopt the modern design language of the ForumLab-modern and Zisco-ERP\nreferences (dark-first), while preserving and extending the in-browser\ncustomization stack.\n\n- app.css: HSL semantic token layer in :root (--primary-h drives the whole\n  accent system), legacy hex vars aliased onto tokens, radius/density scales,\n  component re-skin (buttons/panels/side-nav/pills/focus rings).\n- Member \"Appearance\" (accent hue + density) and per-page \"Sections\" show/hide\n  controls in the Interface panel, persisted to person.uiSettings (dynamic in\n  localStorage, permanent via session defaults) and honored at SSR time on the\n  <html> element and via data-member-hidden, so choices hold without JS.\n- Shared vocabulary in interfaceSettings.js (imported by profile.js and\n  templates.js); app.js mirrors the key lists.\n- Exemplar surfaces (home/social/forum) tagged with data-composer-section +\n  friendly data-section-label.\n- Accent/density/theme render on <html>, not <body>: the :root-declared token\n  layer resolves its nested var(--primary-h) at :root, so a body override is\n  silently ignored.\n- Add UI_ROADMAP.md as the durable in-repo UI reference (the two CodeCanyon\n  templates cannot be vendored); link it from ROADMAP.md and AGENTS.md.\n- Tests: interface-settings.test.js (normalize + SSR round-trip). Docs synced\n  across README/ROADMAP/AGENTS/OPTIMIZATIONS. launch.json autoPort for local dev.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af245b25da7fa592b4c846ddd31256f576160631","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/af245b25da7fa592b4c846ddd31256f576160631"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDU1YTMwOGYwOTk1Y2I5ZTYzZDdhZjQ2YjUxNjY5MTUxMmMzY2E3MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/8664d5e03859bd051d1e7e7dc1c66d7af1757ef9","sha":"8664d5e03859bd051d1e7e7dc1c66d7af1757ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/8664d5e03859bd051d1e7e7dc1c66d7af1757ef9"}],"sha":"55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/55a308f0995cb9e63d7af46b516691512c3ca731"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/8664d5e03859bd051d1e7e7dc1c66d7af1757ef9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T09:27:25Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T09:27:25Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Fix delegate profile identity header and argument-node id leak\n\nDrove Scenario A (Rete Civica Nazionale) through the UI and reviewed the\nmember-facing surfaces against principle-docs/UIReview.md. Two presentation\ndefects fixed:\n\n- Delegate profile header rendered identity as a `label: value` debug dump\n  (Handle/Hash/Role/Status/Bio) with no avatar and the raw hash surfaced as\n  primary identity — the exact anti-pattern the checklist forbids, sitting\n  next to a People directory that renders the same person with an avatar and\n  @handle byline. Rebuilt it to the shared identity block: avatar + @handle\n  with short hash cue + role/status chips.\n- Deliberation argument-map cards leaked a full 36-char UUID\n  (\"Argument id: 93a75b36-...\"). Shortened to a quiet mono cue with the full\n  id on hover, matching the hash-cue pattern used elsewhere.\n\nAdded supporting CSS (.profile-head, .profile-head__name, .chip-row, .mono).\nRegenerated the committed md-assets/party screenshots from the fixed UI.\nLogged the proposal Topic:general classification gap in OPTIMIZATIONS.md.\n\nTests: npm run test:ui green (17 pass, 1 mysql skip); ui/consistency/\ndelegate-profiles focused runs pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c5491c3f8732cf52210d862ac61a1689027d623","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/6c5491c3f8732cf52210d862ac61a1689027d623"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/8664d5e03859bd051d1e7e7dc1c66d7af1757ef9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https:/