ardo Cecchini"},"message":"UI: content-first forum/social redesign, grounded in Scenario A\n\nMove the interface from a neon \"demo dashboard\" to a calm, content-first\nforum/social product, and make evaluating it a standing procedure.\n\nDesign system (src/public/app.css):\n- Retune the palette to a product-grade dark theme with stepped surface tokens\n  instead of glow; drop the body radial gradients and flatten panels/pills.\n- Compact the topbar brand block and slim the operator status strip so pages\n  lead with content, not chrome.\n- Convert the context-panel facts \"label: value\" dump into a quiet inline chip row.\n\nReal feed treatment (discussion/forum/social/People):\n- New renderActorAvatar helper: colour-keyed initial disc, hue stable per actor.\n- Move the @handle byline + timestamp to the card head; colour stance chips so a\n  debate''s shape is legible; add the missing .list-row styling so the People\n  directory renders as an aligned people list with avatars.\n\nBug fixes:\n- Suppress the noisy \"from local-circle\" provenance pill on locally-authored\n  content (renderIssuerPill only fires for genuinely federated issuers).\n- formatTimestamp now emits deterministic dd/mm/yyyy instead of the host''s\n  machine locale (was rendering US m/d/yyyy), fixing Italian content and making\n  SSR output / screenshots reproducible.\n\nDocs & guideline:\n- principle-docs/UIReview.md: default AI UI-evaluation procedure + checklist,\n  with Scenario A (Rete Civica Nazionale) as the standing screenshot/UX lens;\n  linked from AGENTS.md. Logged follow-ups in OPTIMIZATIONS.md.\n- Regenerated md-assets/party and md-assets/walkthrough screenshots.\n- Updated tests/ui.test.js background assertion for the flat themed surface.\n\nFull suite: 203 tests, 200 pass, 3 skipped (MySQL env), 0 fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b4998be8fb7236e6b543b0d8f50cf1edddb9d37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/7b4998be8fb7236e6b543b0d8f50cf1edddb9d37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/68f5959176d5543ecca659d723b6f49cd5aea3d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/68f5959176d5543ecca659d723b6f49cd5aea3d6","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKDY4ZjU5NTkxNzZkNTU0M2VjY2E2NTlkNzIzYjZmNDljZDVhZWEzZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/53b48451486ad47a912280b8a19ddd2d05e36f01","sha":"53b48451486ad47a912280b8a19ddd2d05e36f01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/53b48451486ad47a912280b8a19ddd2d05e36f01"}],"sha":"68f5959176d5543ecca659d723b6f49cd5aea3d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/68f5959176d5543ecca659d723b6f49cd5aea3d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","follower