html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/eb147276a86449272879644bc6b1adf75ef205ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-15T17:03:49Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-15T17:03:49Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Humanize notification labels and resolve remaining raw-hash spots\n\nP1 polish from the UI audit:\n- /notifications now renders human-readable titles via\n  humanizeNotificationType (e.g. \"Proposal created\", \"You were\n  mentioned\") with the raw event type kept only in the pill''s title\n  attribute, instead of leaking machine identifiers like\n  \"petition_created\".\n- Wired the shared @handle resolver into the petition view spots that\n  previously still showed raw hashes: the proposal discussion-feed\n  widget (\"Comment by\"), argument-map nodes, renderUpdatedMeta\n  (\"Updated … by\"), and the freeze frozenBy/moderation lines.\n\nTests: tests/notification-labels.test.js (humanizer mapping + fallback,\nplus an HTTP check that the page shows the label not the raw type).\nFull suite green: 156 non-UI + 18 UI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"149e02a8df15f976e82134769eb40404fa90196b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/149e02a8df15f976e82134769eb40404fa90196b"},"url":"https://a