ents","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/e717ec53b7f1af7ab6d02bf5f0b3e3ec51d5e113/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-21T23:42:23Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-21T23:42:23Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Refocused the UI toward practical user workflows by removing demo/prototype language, tightening module copy, and adding clear guidance on what each lane is for (discussion vs proposals vs social). I updated the home hero and highlights to be goal‑oriented, refreshed verification phrasing, and made empty states more actionable so the modules feel less demonstrative and more operational.\n\nDetails\n\nDiscussion copy and policy messaging now emphasize accountable, topic‑based conversation and decision flow (discussion.html, discussion.js, discussionView.js).\nHome CTA, stats, and highlights now present a pragmatic “workspace” narrative with clearer next actions (home.html).\nSocial, petitions, forum, and module‑disabled panels now include guidance on intended use and next steps (social-wall.html, social-composer.html, petitions-compose.html, forum.html, module-disabled.html).\nDefault brand tagline/footer and empty‑state messaging cleaned up to remove demonstrative tone (templates.js, petitionView.js, forumView.js, socialView.js).\nAdmin posting gate copy now reads as production‑ready (admin.js).\nWallet verification screen copy is now user‑facing with a clear developer shortcut label (auth-eudi.html).\nTests","tree":{"sha":"36d0f7bc4dafd99d6f8cb22503671602dc18b16b","url":"https://api.github.