Q5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/853f5be2d637bcaf1c41091c25776a29b9acad75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-20T16:34:04Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-20T16:34:04Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Implemented per-template composer persistence and expanded the composer tooling to match the demo’s intent: edits now save as global vs per-page override JSON (text/style/dom order), grid drag/drop has clearer horizontal/vertical insertion cues with target highlighting, and a formatting + grid toolbar is available when selections support it. The changes are wired end‑to‑end from server settings through SSR payloads to the composer UI, and styles/validators now allow the new formatting/grid properties.\n\nDetails:\n\nPer-page override storage/rehydration and scope routing (app.js, admin.js, templates.js)\nNew formatting + grid toolbar wiring and allowed style properties (templates.js, app.js, composerView.js)\nGrid drag/drop axis resolution + drop-line visuals and disabled free-move in grid/flex parents (app.js, app.css)\nComposer styling updates + UX polish (app.css)\nDocumentation note about per-template overrides (README.md)\nTests:\n\nnpm run test:ui\nnpm test","tree":{"sha":"9df35a2d02a7d1537dc6f918c8949835bbee78fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/9df35a2d02a7d1537dc6f918c8949835bbee78fc"},"url":"https://ap