node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/bffc96510bfce306008dbb8c4851ac75338daed3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-18T17:37:10Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-18T17:37:10Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Reworked the UI shell to split quick actions (top bar) from a persistent left sidebar with child section links, made the social wall the default post‑login landing, and tucked compose/reply forms behind collapsible panels. Verbose/developer info is now tagged as optional so it can be hidden via theme settings, with the missing module install/uninstall flows captured in the roadmap.\n\nLayout + navigation split and nav state syncing for partial renders in layout.html, navigation.js, app.css, app.js\nWall‑first landing + social feed ordering and compose toggles in home.js, social.js, social.html\nCompose/reply form separation for discussion/forum/petitions/social in discussion.html, forum.html, petitions.html, discussion.js, forum.js, petitions.js, forumView.js, socialView.js\nOptional verbose UI tagging (plus compact mode hook via data-verbosity) across templates like home.html, admin.html, auth-eudi.html, verification-complete.html, app.css\nAdmin section anchors for sidebar child items in admin.html\nRoadmap + optimization notes in ROADMAP.md and OPTIMIZATIONS.md","tree":{"sha":"69d34bad627419c96bb036b494c1d755d46fdd72","url":"htt