5f6456920caf42543f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-14T16:20:36Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-14T16:20:36Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Added peer capability snapshots to ledger gossip so peers can skip disabled endpoints, and surfaced the cached hints in admin/health/peers responses; docs and env config updated alongside a new P2P test.\n\nAdded capabilities.js to build/cache peer capability snapshots (modules + replication + policy/issuer hints) with TTL filtering, used by federation.js, ingest.js, and gossip.js to skip sending/pulling votes/transactions when peers advertise them off.\nAdmin + health now show peer capability hints/counts and /circle/peers returns cached capability hints: admin.js, health.js, circle.js.\nNew P2P test validating capability-based vote skipping: gossip-capabilities.test.js.\nConfig/docs updated for the new TTL knob: config.js, .env.example, README.md, ROADMAP.md, AGENTS.md.\nLogged a new optimization idea related to capability snapshot comparisons in OPTIMIZATIONS.md.","tree":{"sha":"9c25a25d6638e678342d0e8a7f1ea2bc1cf1f9f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/9c25a25d6638e678342d0e8a7f1ea2bc1cf1f9f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/fd8243b043de03ea7fb375f6456920caf42543f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/fd8243b043de03ea7fb375f6456920caf42543f6","node_id":"C_kwDOQpRgi9oAKGZkODI0M2IwNDNkZTAzZWE3ZmIzNzVmNjQ1NjkyMGNhZjQyNTQzZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr/representative-party-web/commit/04a02a62de0e1d1f9151b8fbf3c67d4af5592446","sha":"04a02a62de0e1d1f9151b8fbf3c67d4af5592446","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/04a02a62de0e1d1f9151b8fbf3c67d4af5592446"}],"sha":"fd8243b043de03ea7fb375f6456920caf42543f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/fd8243b043de03ea7fb375f6456920caf42543f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16149805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cekkr","id":16149805,"login":"cekkr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTQ5ODA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cekkr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/commits/04a02a62de0e1d1f9151b8fbf3c67d4af5592446/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-10T06:26:09Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-10T06:26:09Z","email":"rcecchini.ds@gmail.com","name":"Riccardo Cecchini"},"message":"Consolidated visible-entry filtering and follow summaries to cut redundant scans, with a small social feed label tweak for consistency, and logged new optimization ideas.\n\nChanges\n\nAdded predicate-aware visibility helpers plus someVisibleEntries/findVisibleEntry to avoid extra filtering passes, and updated call sites that were doing filterVisibleEntries(...).filter(...) or .find(...) in replication.js, activitypub.js, discussion.js, forum.js, petitions.js, delegateProfiles.js, notifications.js, outbound.js, signatures.js.\nCentralized social follow aggregation with a shared summarizeFollows (includes follower list/counts) and reused it for feed + relationship lookups in followGraph.js and social.js.\nAligned the social feed author fallback label to “anonymous” for UX consistency in socialView.js.\nAdded future optimization ideas for petition comment summarization and follow adjacency indexing in OPTIMIZATIONS.md.\nTests\n\nnpm test (timed out at 120s; failure in “UI social feed supports follows, filters, and reshares” with a Puppeteer wait timeout).\nui.test.js (failed: TimeoutError waiting for filter update, around ui.test.js (line 320)).","tree":{"sha":"b63beaedf592d46ec04421ba83b3883c2b238cd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/trees/b63beaedf592d46ec04421ba83b3883c2b238cd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cekkr/representative-party-web/git/commits/04a02a62de0e1d1f9151b8fbf3c67d4af5592446","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"